Skip draws of no vertices, indices or instances before rasterizer->Draw.
Port of heydemoura/EglantinePS5 39d36b1 (their layer 0019), minus the Bananza terrain macro hook
that is not on this tree. Main only returned early for count/instance 0 on the native_turing path;
every other path still prepared (pipeline, buffers, textures, descriptors) and issued the empty draw.
UpdateTopology still runs first, and the caller-set dirty flags (IndexBuffer) are not cleared, so
the next real draw rebuilds its state. ProcessDrawIndirect is unchanged. Upstream saw ~3% of
Bananza draws empty at Ingot Isle; not measured on this port.
--- a/src/video_core/engines/draw_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/draw_manager.cpp
@@ -324,6 +324,13 @@
                 }
             }
         }
+        // A draw of no vertices, indices or instances writes nothing, but preparing it (pipeline,
+        // buffers, textures, descriptors) costs as much as any other. Topology was updated above;
+        // caller-set dirty flags (index buffer) stay set for the next real draw.
+        if (!instance_count ||
+            !(draw_indexed ? draw_state.index_buffer.count : draw_state.vertex_buffer.count)) {
+            return;
+        }
         maxwell3d.rasterizer->Draw(draw_indexed, instance_count);
     }
 }
